I learned that infosec companies are buying reviews to push their mediocre courses and fool my audience, so I'm launching a promotion campaign for my own Zero Day Engineering training system to raise visibility and remind how it differs:

- My training programs are 100% original content produced by my own first-hand VR work at the frontiers; 

- My attendees include prominent security researchers and I heard them getting $250K bounties with the frameworks that I teach more than once;

- I'm seeing insanely high ratios of repeat and bundle purchases of my high ticket courses; clearly, people are getting the value;

- My company website has a wall of grateful reviews from past attendees, published across all the social platforms;

- I am an active exploit engineer specialized in hardened systems, and happy to share my expertise with paying clients;

- I built a unique universal methodology in 23 years of reverse engineering professionally that works across systems, classes and objectives;

- My methodology proved useful to keep finding bugs in the most difficult systems for well over a decade;

- I don't buy reviews, ads, or distribution - I trust that genuine value will speak for itself;

- I don't build alliances or leverage capital to "beat" other creators - I believe in infinite-sum games, and that every offer has its place on the market;

- I don't force sales or marketing - I let my audience discover my work and make their purchase decisions on their own timelines;

- I run my business solo and take offense personally.

